ongs to, not the app."],"\nA tint is only worth something if a window can't fake it. A phishing page\ndressed in Northwind blue is the attack. So the window manager learns a\nwindow's identity from how it was ",["em",0,"launched"],": it started the process with a\nscoped session and knows the client's pid (",["code",0,"SO_PEERCRED"]," on the Wayland\nsocket). The app is told its identity and draws its own labels. The frame,\nthe band and the taskbar entry come from the compositor, which an app can't\ndraw over."],"\n",["pre",{"class":["shiki","shiki-themes","github-light","github-dark","sk-25qmca"],"tabindex":"0","data-lang":"text"},["code",0,["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"launch (Home, launcher, palm app launch --identity northwind)"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"   │  wm spawns the process with PALM_IDENTITY=<identity id> and a scoped token"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"   │  and records pid → identity"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"   ▼"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"client connects ── wm reads SO_PEERCRED pid ── looks up identity ── tints the frame"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"   │"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"   └─ the app reads PALM_IDENTITY through kit, draws labels, chips and its From card"]]]],"\n",["p",0,"An app the wm did not launch with an identity (a terminal, a foreign app)\ngets no tint and no label. \"No identity\" is a state of its own, never a\ndefault identity."],"\n",["hr",0],"\n",["h2",{"id":"1-the-window-manager"},"1. The window manager"],"\n",["h3",{"id":"the-bar"},"The bar"],"\n",["p",0,"Today (",["code",0,"apps/wm/taskbar.odin"],"):"],"\n",["pre",{"class":["shiki","shiki-themes","github-light","github-dark","sk-25qmca"],"tabindex":"0","data-lang":"text"},["code",0,["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"}